{
  "id": "COMPOUND:16888 - PROTEIN:4035",
  "verbalization": "Theasaponin E1 is implicated in the activation of Calcium/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase type IV through multiple indirect pathways. The core mechanism involves the compound acting as a target of 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline, which is itself a target of Theasaponin E1. This quinoline compound is linked to the phosphatidylinositol 4-phosphate 3-kinase C2 domain-containing subunit beta, which in turn targets Calcium/calmodulin-dependent protein kinase type IV. Additionally, Theasaponin E1 is also linked to K-252a, which similarly targets the same kinase. These pathways suggest that Theasaponin E1 exerts its effects through a common downstream target, 4-(3-Pyridin-2-Yl-1h-Pyrazol-4-Yl)Quinoline, which may act as a bridge between the compound and the kinase. The evidence supports a mechanism where Theasaponin E1 indirectly activates the kinase via a shared target, highlighting a potential role in signaling pathways involving calcium and calmodulin.",
